course: dictionary
lesson: 12642
title: Dispersal: spreading out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dispersal is a noun. It comes from the verb disperse, which means to scatter or spread out. Dispersal is the act of spreading things over a wide area, or of a group breaking up.
explain: In science, «seed dispersal» means how plants spread their seeds. Think of it as a plant sending its seeds somewhere new, so they do not all grow in one crowded spot.
explain: The same word can describe people. Police may order the «dispersal of the crowd», which means telling the crowd to break up and go in different directions. Ask yourself: is something being spread over a wide area, or is a group breaking up? If yes, the word is dispersal.
fact: Dispersal is a noun. You can write a dispersal, but it is usually uncountable: dispersal of seeds.
fact: Disperse is the verb: to scatter or spread out.
fact: «Seed dispersal» means how plants spread their seeds.
fact: Seeds can be dispersed by wind, water, animals or bursting pods.
fact: «The dispersal of the crowd» means the crowd breaks up and goes off in different directions.
exercise: «Seed dispersal helps plants grow in new places.» What does dispersal mean here? | Digging up the plants | Counting the seeds in a packet | *Spreading seeds out over a wide area | Watering the garden
exercise: The police asked for the «dispersal of the crowd». What did they want? | Everyone to sit down on the grass | Everyone to form a bigger crowd | *The crowd to break up and go in different directions | A song to start
exercise: Which word is the verb that goes with dispersal? | dispersal | disperser | dispersed | *disperse
test: «Dispersal by wind» means seeds are carried by what? | Rain clouds | Animals' fur | Bursting pods | *The wind
test: In «seed dispersal by animals», who does the spreading? | Teachers | Tall trees | *Animals | Rain clouds
exam: Which phrase means how plants spread their seeds? | *Seed dispersal | Seed colour | Seed weight | Seed shelter
